import Mathlib

namespace ReaderA

open MeasureTheory Pointwise

/-- A convex body in `ℝⁿ`: a compact convex set with nonempty interior. -/
def IsConvexBody {n : ℕ} (K : Set (Fin n → ℝ)) : Prop :=
  Convex ℝ K ∧ IsCompact K ∧ (interior K).Nonempty

/-- The lattice `Λ = A ℤⁿ` generated by the columns of the matrix `A`. When `det A ≠ 0` this is
a full-rank lattice, and every full-rank lattice in `ℝⁿ` is of this form. -/
def latticeOf {n : ℕ} (A : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) : Set (Fin n → ℝ) :=
  Set.range fun z : Fin n → ℤ => A.mulVec (fun i => (z i : ℝ))

/-- Theorem 1.1: there is an absolute constant `C > 0` such that for every integer `n ≥ 2` and
every convex body `K ⊂ ℝⁿ` some full-rank lattice `Λ = A ℤⁿ` (`det A ≠ 0`) satisfies
`K + Λ = ℝⁿ` and `vol_n(K) / det Λ ≤ C n log n`, where `det Λ = |det A|` is the covolume.
The inequality is stated multiplied out, `vol_n(K) ≤ C n log n · |det A|`, in `ℝ≥0∞`. -/
theorem reading_thm_1_1 :
    ∃ C : ℝ, 0 < C ∧ ∀ n : ℕ, 2 ≤ n → ∀ K : Set (Fin n → ℝ), IsConvexBody K →
      ∃ A : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ, A.det ≠ 0 ∧
        K + latticeOf A = Set.univ ∧
        volume K ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (C * n * Real.log n * |A.det|) := by
  sorry

end ReaderA

/-
Ambiguities and choices.

1. ℝⁿ: `Fin n → ℝ` with Mathlib's `volume` (product Lebesgue measure = n-dimensional Lebesgue
   measure vol_n). Its topology (sup norm) is the Euclidean topology, so "compact" and
   "interior" are the usual ones; `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)` would give the same statement.
2. Convex body: the source's definition "compact with nonempty interior" plus convexity:
   `Convex ℝ K ∧ IsCompact K ∧ (interior K).Nonempty`. No symmetry or regularity assumed.
3. Full-rank lattice Λ and det Λ: written by hand as Λ = A ℤⁿ with A an n×n real matrix,
   det A ≠ 0, and det Λ = |det A| (the covolume, i.e. the volume of the fundamental
   parallelepiped). This is independent of the choice of basis and every full-rank lattice
   (discrete subgroup spanning ℝⁿ) arises so; it is equivalent to Mathlib's `IsZLattice` with
   `ZLattice.covolume`. I quantify over A rather than over Λ to avoid defining covolume as a
   function of a set.
4. K + Λ = ℝⁿ: pointwise Minkowski sum of sets `K + latticeOf A = Set.univ`.
5. vol(K)/det Λ ≤ C n log n: multiplied out as vol(K) ≤ C n log n · |det A| (|det A| > 0, so
   equivalent), and kept in ℝ≥0∞ via `ENNReal.ofReal`, so no `toReal` of a possibly infinite
   measure and no division (vol(K) is finite anyway since K is compact). For n ≥ 2,
   log n ≥ log 2 > 0, so the right side is a genuine positive real; log is natural (Real.log).
6. "absolute constant C > 0": ∃ C quantified before n and K. "one full-rank lattice" read as
   "some (at least one)" lattice.
7. The infimum θ_L(K) in the definition is not needed for Theorem 1.1 as stated (it would
   follow as θ_L(K) ≤ C n log n); I state the theorem's explicit lattice form, avoiding an
   `sInf`.
-/
